      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T13:29:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we build a temporary bitmap of unavailable slots and then select the first free bit? The nested search scans every child for each candidate, making allocation quadratic as occupancy grows. A 2,048-bit bitmap needs 256 bytes and avoids maintaining persistent allocation state. We’d need to preserve the checks for pending-old SAs and the remote rekey bit.",
      "revId": "45c21c7c71c770fcef9e44f604893e85914aa258",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
