        "id": 3383
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-24T11:08:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PS4 uses a temporary 2,048-bit stack bitmap (256 bytes). It marks live and pending-old IDs in one Child scan, checks local and remote ID prefixes separately, and retains the remote rekey bit when matching the remote prefix. The first clear slot is selected in at most 32 uword scans on 64-bit systems; no persistent allocator state is added. Existing Delete/rekey collision tests pass under debug/ASAN.",
      "parentUuid": "2d6c5369_4a430af4",
      "revId": "45c21c7c71c770fcef9e44f604893e85914aa258",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
